    },
    {
      "arcId": "S4FMZX2BSRAD5C4KIZ45CILTRI",
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "subhead",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "4",
      "subhead_level": 2,
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "arcId": "WLANJGK3NVF7RP7YBJNQF2LMT4",
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>The House Oversight Committee voted to subpoena Attorney General Pam Bondi.</b>",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "arcId": "VBI6PMZJ2FAVVON656JLWAESVM",
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<b>Why?</b> To face questions on the Justice Department’s handling of the release of files about sex offender Jeffrey Epstein. Some lawmakers accuse Bondi of <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2026/02/26/justice-department-epstein-trump-allegations/\">botching the release</a>.",
        "<b>What now? </b>It’s not clear how Bondi will respond to the subpoena. But the vote <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/03/04/house-oversight-committee-subpoenas-attorney-general-pam-bondi/\">is likely to set up another clash</a> between House Republicans and the White House over Epstein."
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "ad",
      "breakpoints": [
        "large"
      ],
      "kind": "block",
      "size": "medium",
      "adPath": "/the-seven",
      "primarySectionID": "/topics/the-seven",
      "position": {
        "large": "incontent_1"
      }
    },
    {
      "arcId": "LELVWPSJ3BGPVKSL6EULUAO6FA",
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "subhead",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "5",
      "subhead_level": 2,
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "arcId": "MLAIRSQ675EFZE4F3CJ6MDQQK4",
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>A new poll shows that trust in major U.S. health agencies is declining.</b>",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "arcId": "XJFT73DKSNHKRJUJVE6W7MQ5W4",
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<b>Key finding: </b>Roughly 6 in 10 people say they trust the CDC, FDA and NIH, <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2026/03/05/rfk-jr-health-leaders-trust-issue/\">according to the survey</a>. In 2024, roughly three-quarters of people said they trusted those agencies.",
        "<b>In related news:</b> Health Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. has been pushing medical schools to boost nutrition education. More than 50 of them <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2026/03/05/medical-school-nutrition-training-rfk/\">will pledge to do so today</a>.",
        "<b>One more thing:</b> Kennedy has <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/03/04/kennedy-vs-dunkin-donuts/\">declared war on Dunkin’</a>."
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "arcId": "LELVWPSJ3BGPVKSL6EULUAO6FA",
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "subhead",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "6",
      "subhead_level": 2,
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "arcId": "CSE77WIHBBF3BDXRWCAQN3L5QY",
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>Should you take a supplement for heart health? Here’s what the science says.</b>",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "imageURL": "https://arc-anglerfish-washpost-prod-washpost.s3.amazonaws.com/public/OFMW4SQFPGLMHS2DYKIRS6UFTQ_size-normalized.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 6720,
      "imageHeight": 4480,
      "image_type": "photograph",
      "widthFactor": "full-bleed",
      "fullcaption": "A lot of supplements claim to help your heart. But the list of those that actually may be beneficial is short, experts say. (Andrea Arevalo/For The Washington Post)",
      "blurb": "A lot of supplements claim to help your heart. But the list of those that actually may be beneficial is short, experts say."
    },
    {
      "arcId": "DAOJPSAYOBBVFKFCDHJ6C64JNA",
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<b>According to experts:</b> Supplements like fish oil or magnesium can’t treat or prevent heart conditions like medication can. See evidence for and against six supplements <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/wellness/2026/03/05/dietary-supplements-heart-cardiovascular-health/\">here</a>.",
        "<b>What to do instead:</b> Get plenty of exercise each week, don’t smoke and make sure you have a well-balanced diet. To get started, try to adopt <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/wellness/2023/02/14/centenarians-healthy-eating-habits/\">these four healthy eating habits</a>."
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "ad",
      "breakpoints": [
        "small"
      ],
